## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / objective / wound-and-meal
Is being hurt the same as doing wrong?
What is the nature of evil?

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / entry fallback / wound-and-meal
Augustine explains evil as damage to, or loss of, something good. Compare a wound with stealing a meal: suffering harm is not the same as choosing to harm someone.

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / completion/ending / wound-and-meal
An injury is harm suffered; stealing a meal is harm chosen. Augustine treats both as losses of goodness, but distinguishes suffering from wrongdoing.

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / story body / wound-and-meal
Augustine explains evil as damage to, or loss of, something good. Compare a wound with stealing a meal: suffering harm is not the same as choosing to harm someone.

