Northern Italy, thirteenth century

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / objective / reason-and-fire
Whose fault is fire?
What can reason tell us about God?

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / entry fallback / reason-and-fire
The next morning, the study desk is ready for a comparison with Aquinas. Compare Aquinas's fire example with the argument you just made. Fire can function as fire while harming something else. Consider what that challenges and which questions about suffering remain unanswered.

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / completion/ending / reason-and-fire
Aquinas says fire can function well as fire while harming something else. That challenges the claim that harm must come from a wholly evil source, but leaves the creator's responsibility in question.

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / story body / reason-and-fire
