## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / objective / three-and-one
Does being Son mean being less divine?
How can three be one God?

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / entry fallback / three-and-one
It is evening. We clear the desk to consider what Christians mean by the Trinity. Augustine's earlier text is now compared with Aquinas's limits on proof. Clarify the Christian claim of one God as Father, Son and Holy Spirit without treating human examples as proof of that belief.

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / completion/ending / three-and-one
Augustine distinguishes Father, Son and Holy Spirit while affirming one God. Aquinas says observation of created things cannot prove this belief.

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / skip bridge / three-and-one
Augustine distinguishes Father, Son and Holy Spirit while affirming one God. Aquinas says observation of created things cannot prove this belief.

