## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / objective / hands-and-book
What does this bodily rite tell us about creation?
Does rejecting worldly desires mean rejecting people?

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / entry fallback / hands-and-book
The Lyon ritual is a separate medieval text. Its ceremony uses hands and a Gospel book while claiming a spiritual gift. Examine what those physical actions do, and what they cannot establish about the community's beliefs about creation.

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / completion/ending / hands-and-book
The Lyon rite uses hands and a Gospel book while promising a spiritual gift. The candidate also promises to reject worldly desires and love enemies. These commitments do not tell us everything the community believed about creation.

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / story body / hands-and-book
