## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / completion/ending / bread-and-body
Aquinas says the bread becomes Christ's body while its appearance and taste remain. A change in appearance would therefore not be the test of his claim.

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / skip bridge / bread-and-body
Aquinas distinguishes what the bread is from how it appears. He says the first changes while the second remains.

