Why help if help does not earn salvation?
Are these writers asking the same question about grace?
What is bodily discipline for?

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / entry fallback / gift-and-neighbour
Luther says that good deeds do not earn acceptance by God. At this desk, consider why he still calls people to serve their neighbours and practise bodily discipline.

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / completion/ending / gift-and-neighbour
For Luther, helping neighbours and practising self-discipline matter. They serve people and train conduct, but do not buy acceptance by God.

## divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7 / skip bridge / gift-and-neighbour
For Luther, caring for a neighbour serves a real need without earning God's acceptance. The later role of good deeds remains disputed.

